Negative control — the DIFF-ONLY update body (AC-23, fix 8c, parity row L3).

Mutates `update`'s body from `mapIAddressDataDiff(data, baseData)` to
`mapIAddressData(data)`, so a save sends the WHOLE model instead of only the
fields that moved. The PUT still goes out, to the same url, with the same
method, and still succeeds — it just re-sends every field the user never
touched, which is the legacy-parity claim L3 exists to hold.

Declared AC — AC-23: "saving an edit sends only the changed fields". The
read-back asserts the captured PUT body has EXACTLY the changed key(s) and does
NOT contain `country_id`; asserting the request succeeded does not
discriminate.

Should flip RED — all three AC-23 read-backs in
__tests__/client-address.manager-save.int.test.ts:
  - "AC-23 puts ONLY the changed field and does NOT re-send the unchanged
     country"
  - "AC-23 sends nothing at all beyond the fields that actually moved"
  - "AC-22/AC-23 puts the chosen address type on the wire when the type is what
     changed"

No collateral beyond that set. This is the complement of
`client-address.manager-amputation.must-fail.patch`, which reds the same three
by removing the update LIMB entirely: that one proves the PUT is reached, this
one proves the body it carries is a diff. Two capabilities, two mutants.

